    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 0,
        "sourceEnd": 192,
        "text": "Good morning, everyone. Today I'm going to talk about the number of people who visited our town library over the last five years. I have a simple chart here, and I'll describe the main trends.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "287fe16ba3b6d2fdbb84b7fd3bf17a74dd1dab92606b14cef34f1cd1a0a15f18",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 194,
        "sourceEnd": 671,
        "text": "First, let's look at the total number of visits per year. In 2019, there were 20,000 visits. In 2020, the number dropped to 12,000. That's a decrease of 8,000 visits, or 40 percent. Then, in 2021, the number went up to 15,000. So there was an increase of 3,000 visits, which is 25 percent compared to 2020. In 2022, the number rose again to 18,000. That's an increase of 20 percent from 2021. Finally, in 2023, the number reached 22,000. That's a 22 percent increase from 2022.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "5d446437ef606c9252a8f98765f37d85f767204b11a536241077f2c82d2fd949",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.8
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 673,
        "sourceEnd": 1015,
        "text": "Now, let's compare different age groups in 2023. The largest group was children under 12. There were 8,000 visits by this group. The second largest group was teenagers, with 5,000 visits. Adults aged 20 to 59 made 6,000 visits. And seniors, people over 60, made 3,000 visits. So children were the biggest group, and seniors were the smallest.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0f45e554af0a3bf792ce43e3db51599d2aeb77d64f7127c686c433c24064dffb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.8
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 1017,
        "sourceEnd": 1256,
        "text": "What about the most popular days? In 2023, Saturday was the busiest day, with 1,200 visits. Sunday was the second busiest, with 1,000 visits. On weekdays, the average was only 400 visits per day. So weekends were much busier than weekdays.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "26c9af2243a8b4be2753fce8c8e4a0a17a4bbf9bbfdd8296777ea1647766901a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.8
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 1258,
        "sourceEnd": 1474,
        "text": "Finally, let's look at the number of books borrowed. In 2019, people borrowed 30,000 books. In 2023, they borrowed 45,000 books. That's an increase of 15,000, or 50 percent. So book borrowing grew faster than visits.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "bd5ae580338eb9fc816e8c61d26a63743e187f76943720babfa2021a0c053e23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.8
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 1476,
        "sourceEnd": 1678,
        "text": "To sum up, library visits decreased in 2020 but then increased steadily. Children are the main users, and weekends are the busiest times. Book borrowing has risen significantly. Thank you for listening.",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f073d4ade83a2658b334f0e7929e8290fd7b7adca8ee40fb5b13e84911807b9e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.8
      }
    ]
  },
